  "source": {
    "body": "## Why\n\nREADME.md:34-38 commits to extracting legal clauses into stable tracked-variable records, and `docs/contracts/tracked-variable-v1.md:15` defines the record, with extractors owned by domain repos. In this repo `ingest_document` (`src/doc_lineage/ingest.py:242`) stops at a segments artifact plus evidence files, `export-fact-key-map` (`src/doc_lineage/cli.py:72`, `src/doc_lineage/export/fact_key_map.py:16`) only consumes already-authored records, and its fixture `tests/fixtures/fact_key_map/tracked_variables.json` has identities without source evidence. `vocab/legal-clauses.json:20` defines keys such as `legal.fees.management_rate`, but nothing produces a value for them from text. Verified by inspecting the ingest publisher, CLI dispatch and fact-map producer: no extractor or entry point exists. This is a missing capability; schema and vocabulary tests prove components, not a source-to-claim path.\n\nCurrent source readback: `src/doc_lineage/ingest.py:242` at `b9daca70b27f452d62d8c6ccdb3bcd3b5dc7a783` (file SHA-256 `891d8cb788a9f215233f88b3dcb53e812377d19d8b63c510ac5a0d6c7296bcbb`). Earlier detailed line ranges and reproductions retain their reviewed-commit provenance; intervening anchor changes were checked for relevance.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A bounded extractor over ingested segments and evidence that emits `tracked-variable/v1` records for explicitly supported clauses, starting with the management fee in `tests/fixtures/synthetic_lpa.pdf`.\n- A CLI entry point that publishes the records with evidence references and manifest hashes.\n- Unsupported or ambiguous text is reported as unresolved, never as an asserted value.\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- Do not claim all 25 ontology keys, arbitrary legal language or consultant-report extraction are solved by the initial subset.\n- Do not move extraction into the identity-map exporter, alter fleet schemas, add cloud or model dependencies, or build the downstream renderer.\n- Do not edit `vocab/legal-clauses.json` keys.\n- Scaffold-only completion does NOT count: records copied from a pre-authored fixture, or a value not derived from segment text, fail this issue.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] Document supported clause forms, identity rules and unresolved behavior in `docs/contracts/tracked-variable-v1.md` (new \"Extraction coverage\" section).\n- [ ] In `src/doc_lineage/ingest.py` (after `ingest_document`, line 294), add a function that reads `segments.json` and evidence objects from an ingest run and returns tracked-variable records keyed by `legal.fees.management_rate` via `src/doc_lineage/vocab.py` (`load_legal_clauses`).\n- [ ] In `src/doc_lineage/cli.py` (parser near line 72-77, dispatch at `main` lines 137-162), add an `extract-variables` subcommand that writes validated records and a manifest to a new output directory.\n- [ ] Validate each record against `docs/contracts/schemas/tracked-variable-v1.schema.json` and each evidence reference against `evidence-object-v1.schema.json` before publishing.\n- [ ] Add tests to `tests/ingest/test_ingest_synthetic_pdf.py` ingesting `tests/fixtures/synthetic_lpa.pdf`, plus changed-fee and ambiguous-clause cases using `tests/fixtures/mutations/management_fee_bump/`.\n- [ ] Add a test in `tests/export/test_fact_key_map.py` feeding extractor output to `export_fact_key_map` (`src/doc_lineage/export/fact_key_map.py:50`).\n- [ ] Update README.md:34-38 and `docs/fact-key-map.md:25` to describe the extractor and how to inspect unresolved clauses.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `pytest tests/ingest/test_ingest_synthetic_pdf.py -k tracked_variable` passes: the synthetic LPA yields `legal.fees.management_rate` with a value taken from source text, not from a fixture.\n- [ ] Published records validate against `tracked-variable-v1.schema.json` and evidence quotes, page locator, original digest and manifest hashes match the emitted files.\n- [ ] Deliberate-break gate: temporarily hard-code the extracted value in the new extractor in `src/doc_lineage/ingest.py`; the changed-fee test must FAIL. Revert afterward.\n- [ ] An ambiguous or unsupported clause produces an unresolved entry and no asserted value, and `pytest tests/export/test_fact_key_map.py` passes using extractor output.\n\n## Implementation Notes\n\n- `src/doc_lineage/ingest.py:242`, `src/doc_lineage/cli.py:72`, `:137-162`.\n- `src/doc_lineage/export/fact_key_map.py:16`, `src/doc_lineage/vocab.py`.\n- `vocab/legal-clauses.json:20`, `docs/contracts/tracked-variable-v1.md:15`, `docs/fact-key-map.md:25`.\n- `tests/fixtures/synthetic_lpa.pdf`, `tests/fixtures/mutations/management_fee_bump/before_segments.json` and `tests/fixtures/mutations/management_fee_bump/after_segments.json`.\n- `tests/fixtures/fact_key_map/tracked_variables.json`, `tests/export/test_fact_key_map.py`.\n- Execution authority: the owner released the intake hold on 2026-10-16 (recorded decision, Claude Code campaign session). Auto-pilot, keepalive and runner assignment are permitted for this issue under the normal priority order.\n\n<!-- repo-review-finding: stranske/Doc-Lineage#175cfc2c6674 -->\n\n<!-- repo-review-item: stranske/Doc-Lineage#175cfc2c6674 -->\n\n",
